WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight i
a Golden Globe-nominated actor

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
and director you know
from films such as "Loving,"

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Zero Dark Thirty,"
and "Boy Erased."

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stars in
"The Underground Railroad,

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.542 size:81% position:41%
which is streaming now
on Amazon Prime Video.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
our friend Joel Edgerton.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:14.814 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Joel?

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very good, mate.
I've missed you.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-But I'm fine.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:21.521
-You know, I hope you know I'm
not just blowing smoke here.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
As happy as I am
that you're on the show,

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:27.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is very bittersweet
that you're not here in person

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.496 line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah, it is actually.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.032 line:92%
I'd love to give you a man hug

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
and run in
and have a studio audience

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.706
-It must be pretty boring
without a studio audience.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:43.643
-I would be giving you a man hug
in congratulations.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a new dad.
Congratulations, Joel.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, thank you.
I'm very excited.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:56.823
It's one of the great
silver linings of the last year.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sort of a crazy terrible year.
I'm very happy.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a perfect, perfect
silver lining.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also know
that you're back in Australia.

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.833
Thank you for waking up at
the crack of dawn to talk to us.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.836
And you're back doing a project,
and I imagine Australia

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
is very proud
of your accomplishments,

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:14.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
but knowing what I know
about Australians,

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
they also probably
want to check in with you

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make sure you're not
getting too full of yourself

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.681 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, I am.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughter ]
-I am.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact, full to the brim,
some might say.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- This is very --
Oh, look at that!

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.594 line:92%
You got the mug we sent you.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, by the way.
Thank you.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.365 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is really --
I feel like this is really

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.802 line:92%
helping our at-home audience

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
who misses being
in the same room.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.807
-Just trying to bring back
the old feeling, you know?

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, I want to talk to yo
about your TV show,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.312
but there's a show that we'r
sort of obsessed with here

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.414 line:92%
called "Tiny Secret Whispers,"

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
which stars
a different Australian actor

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the same spelling
of your name

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.121 line:92%
pronounced Joel "Edgar-ton."

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.456 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Do you know him?

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Sighs ] Yeah.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've run into him a coupl
of times at "events," you know

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:15.468
You know, it took me a --
I've had a bit of a --

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.371
It's been a long ride,
but I've gotten used to the idea

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:23.409
that he's masquerading somewhat,
at least on paper, as me.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.511 line:92%
-Has there ever been a situation

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.313
where you've really wanted
a part, and he's got it,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
but for a moment,
there's confusion

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.918 line:92%
and you think it's yours?

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.086 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Well, yeah, I mean,

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:37.957
I did get asked to auditio
for "Tiny Secret Whispers.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:42.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
I tried to download
the Pumpkin...

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Butternut.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:46.099 line:92%
-Butternut streaming site.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:49.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I had a lot of problem
with an Australian credit card

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know --
Look. To be honest,

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've checked out
a couple of clips,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I love the actor
that plays...

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.978 line:92%
I'm not a fan of Joel Edgar-ton.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:02:59.679 line:92%
-Yeah, well, that's fine.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.849 size:84% position:42%
I mean, I would imagine
that's hard for you.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ] I want to ask
about a real TV show

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were in,
the real Joel Edgerton.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:13.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your first TV gig,
you did not last long.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:16.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your character, I should say
did not last long.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No. [ Laughs ]

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:22.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
My first acting job
out of drama school,

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
I played Ben Mendelsohn's
younger brother,

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were holding up
a video store.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:32.278
Half the audience maybe wanted
to know what a video store is.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:35.315 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I was dead by 11:00 a.m.

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:39.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
on my first day on my job
as an actor.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
11:00 a.m.
-That's not great.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.991 size:88% position:44%
-I thought, "This is the
beginning of my career."

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was in my car
driving home going,

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:51.431
"I just quit my regular jo
for this, and now I'm dead."

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.699 line:92%
-You mention Ben Mendelsohn.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:55.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I love both of you
as actors, and I mean that

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I first saw you in a film,
"Animal Kingdom,"

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
where both of you didn't reall
end up living very long.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:05.445
Have you ever been in a projec
with Ben where either of you

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:10.250 size:75% position:38%
have made it through
the full run time?

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:14.454 line:92%
-No. "The King," we both die

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.723 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Uh, spoiler alert.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.459 line:92%
I think you've hit on something.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think Ben and I
are destined --

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's sort of Romeo and Juliet,
right?

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:27.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Yeah. You are the
Australian Romeo and Juliet.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:31.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It'd be like,
"Yeah, come on, mate, let's...

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.338 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Blegh."

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.573 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was a really,
really good impression

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Ben Mendelsohn
as either Romeo or Juliet.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:41.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, I do want to ask abou
"Underground Railroad."

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:44.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back with mor
from Joel Edgerton.

